## What is is social enginnering attack and what does it look like?
Social enginnering attack involves one or scammers maniplulating the victim into giving up vital information such as bank details, SIN number, login credentials. 
They achieve this by having the victim download some suspicious softwares which could lead to various different types of malware, have they viste dangerous sites, or
have the victim themselves give up their credentials through various means. Social enginnering attack dones't necessarily have to take place in the web all the time,
they could be in person too!. And with how rapid ai is evolving and growing, it has certainly became a part a much more powerful tool for deception. Here are some 
common examples of different attacks:
- Phishing which involves using messages to get the victim to share sensitive information
- Baiting which invloves the promise of a reward in exchange of sensitive information
- Scareware which involves a malware that scares the user to give up sensistive information by pretending to be some type of higher authority or support
- Ai base attack which involves using ai deepfake to generate videos of trusted individuals or mimic their voice

### Even companies are not safe 
Scammers don't just target indviduals, but companies as well. Sometimes it's better to target companies as they offer better rewards even if the risk of getting caught
is higher. This can have devasting impact for the companies and more importantant their consumers. In 2025 their were 14 data breaches involving more then 1 million 
healthcare records. This affected over 20 million U.S residents. Emails pretending to be healthcare personnel were sent to over 79 healthcare providers just in 2024. 
These attack costes an average of $9 million USD with 515 to 494326 patients affected from malfunction of medical devices due to these attacks. BMO was also a victim 
to these attacks in 2018. A data breach lead to scammers claiming to have important data in their possession. Follow by this was a wave of phishing and malware 
attacks for months. 

#### How to spot attacks and protect yourself
There are various signs to look out for, some obvious and some not so much. But always keep an eye out for:
- Hidden links
- People claiming to be government personnel
- Unknown QR codes
- Bad spelling and grammars 
- Login pages from unknown sites 
What are some ways to protect outselves? The best thing to do is always do research before hand and be vigilant. Never blinding trust everything you see. Here are
other ways to protect yourself:
- Contact the organization the person is claiming to be
- Install sercurity tools like antiviruses 
- Backup your files regularly
- Use multifactor authentication 
- Limit the information you post online

